    "narrative": "The LawDog lineup is anchored today by **Matt Chapman**, who carries the day\u2019s highest projection at 68.48. His status as the leadoff hitter against a shaky E-Rod (4.68 xERA) provides significant volume, compounded by an elite BvP profile that suggests he\u2019s comfortable seeing the ball out of the southpaw's hand today. Similarly, **Dylan Beavers** (65.55) and **Taylor Ward** (62.85) benefit from an advantageous matchup against Burke, utilizing strong park factors to bolster their ceilings. **Geraldo Perdomo** rounds out our tier of \"strong\" plays; his promotion to the #2 spot significantly elevates his value in our 5x5 format, as his projected stolen base contributions make him essential in today\u2019s tight scoring environment.\n\nThe bench decision for today was tight, as **Cal Raleigh** (58.11) barely qualified for the active roster despite a sub-60 score. While **Daulton Varsho** was considered, he was ultimately excluded due to a combination of a tough matchup against Manaea and the assumption that he is not in the confirmed lineup. We are closely monitoring **Bryson Stott** (52.49); while he remains a starter, he faces a negative SP skill adjustment against Ashcraft, meaning he is on a short leash if the early innings suggest a struggle against the slider. We are also keeping an eye on our deeper bench\u2014including **Jonathan Aranda**, **Gleyber Torres**, **Masyn Winn**, **Brendan Donovan**, **Jung Hoo Lee**, **Jeremiah Jackson**, **Gavin Sheets**, **Drew Gilbert**, **Ryan Waldschmidt**, and **Yainer Diaz**\u2014to ensure we aren't leaving production on the table, though **Jos\u00e9 Ram\u00edrez** and **Will Smith** remain locked on the IL, frustrating our overall lineup depth. **Tyler Freeman** is currently off the board, and we advise caution regarding the potential for late-game defensive substitutions in the outfield which could shorten the ceilings for **Lawrence Butler** and **Taylor Ward**.",
